		<section>
			<h2>Download</h2>
			<p class="muted">Version <%= feed.version %> · <a href="<%= feed.notes %>">Release notes</a></p>

			<h3>macOS (Apple silicon)</h3>
			<p><a href="<%= feed.url( Marktone::Installer.mac ) %>">↓ Marktone-arm64.dmg</a> <span class="muted"><%= feed.size( Marktone::Installer.mac ) %> · <a href="<%= feed.checksum_url( Marktone::Installer.mac ) %>">SHA-256</a></span></p>
			<p>Open the <code>.dmg</code> and drag Marktone into Applications. The first time, right-click Marktone in Applications and choose Open: Marktone is not notarised by Apple, so macOS refuses a plain double-click.</p>

			<h3>Linux (x86-64)</h3>
			<p><a href="<%= feed.url( Marktone::Installer.appimage ) %>">↓ Marktone-x86_64.AppImage</a> <span class="muted"><%= feed.size( Marktone::Installer.appimage ) %> · <a href="<%= feed.checksum_url( Marktone::Installer.appimage ) %>">SHA-256</a></span><br>Make it executable with <code>chmod +x Marktone-x86_64.AppImage</code>, then run it.</p>
			<p><a href="<%= feed.url( Marktone::Installer.deb ) %>">↓ Marktone-amd64.deb</a> <span class="muted"><%= feed.size( Marktone::Installer.deb ) %> · <a href="<%= feed.checksum_url( Marktone::Installer.deb ) %>">SHA-256</a></span><br>On Debian or Ubuntu: <code>sudo apt install ./Marktone-amd64.deb</code></p>
			<p><a href="<%= feed.url( Marktone::Installer.tarball ) %>">↓ Marktone-x86_64.tar.gz</a> <span class="muted"><%= feed.size( Marktone::Installer.tarball ) %> · <a href="<%= feed.checksum_url( Marktone::Installer.tarball ) %>">SHA-256</a></span><br>Unpack it and run <code>marktone</code> in the unpacked folder; its desktop file and icon are beside it.</p>
		</section>
